Tie off unconnected SPI ports in every config (AbstractConfig).

Adds WithSPITiedOff to AbstractConfig's harness binders, as the RiskyBird
Chipyard fork did, so every config built on AbstractConfig defines its SPI
inputs until a board binder overrides them. Generic, but it changes the
harness of every upstream config with a SPI port, so whether it belongs here
or only in RiskyBird's own configs is an open decision.

diff --git a/generators/chipyard/src/main/scala/config/AbstractConfig.scala b/generators/chipyard/src/main/scala/config/AbstractConfig.scala
index 30bcf0ec..4fd7a2b6 100644
--- a/generators/chipyard/src/main/scala/config/AbstractConfig.scala
+++ b/generators/chipyard/src/main/scala/config/AbstractConfig.scala
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ class AbstractConfig extends Config(
   new chipyard.harness.WithGPIOPinsTiedOff ++                      /** tie-off chiptop GPIO-pins, if GPIO-punchthrough is used */
   new chipyard.harness.WithGPIOTiedOff ++                          /** tie-off chiptop GPIOs, if GPIOs are present */
   new chipyard.harness.WithI2CTiedOff ++                           /** tie-off i2c ports if present */
+  new chipyard.harness.WithSPITiedOff ++                           /** define SPI inputs until a board binder connects them */
   new chipyard.harness.WithSimSPIFlashModel ++                     /** add simulated SPI flash memory, if SPI is enabled */
   new chipyard.harness.WithSimAXIMMIO ++                           /** add SimAXIMem for axi4 mmio port, if enabled */
   new chipyard.harness.WithTieOffInterrupts ++                     /** tie-off interrupt ports, if present */
